**Proposed replacement for:** [accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).
That accepted record remains unchanged; this proposal needs the support desk's acceptance.

## Context

[The #4471 investigation](/kb/incidents/4471-split) shows that subject matching hid a separate
form-hint bug in a parser ticket. Intake tags also disagree with tenant-aware classification.

## Decision proposed

Read the body, resolve the tenant, determine date order and form, then classify using
`causeOf`. Merge only when `sameCause` is true. Subject matching can find candidate tickets,
but cannot authorize a merge. Unknown tenants and unexplained symptoms stay unmerged for
investigation. Count each report ID once and keep membership auditable.

## Consequences

Triage requires more context than a subject comparison. Different subjects can share one cause;
the same subject can require separate tickets. Fixing the parser and fixing the form hint are
separate engineering tasks. Recheck uncertain reports against actual input and output.

